ed or unsupported status value.\",\n     \"when\": \"The client calls GET /api/requests with that status filter.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 400, the response message is \\\"Status must be Open, In progress, or Done.\\\", and response field errors.status contains \\\"Unsupported status filter.\\\"\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-1.4\",\n     \"given\": \"The database operation for loading the request list fails after startup.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client calls GET /api/requests.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 500 and the response message is \\\"Could not load requests.\\\"\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n   \"ears\": \"When a client sends a valid POST /api/requests body, the Maintenance Requests API shall create and return HTTP 201 with a positive system-assigned id, UTC createdAt, trimmed title and description, and Open status, ignore caller-supplied id, createdAt, or status values, omit an absent or blank-after-trimming description, and return HTTP 500 with message \\\"Could not create the request.\\\" if creation fails.\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\"\n   ],\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.1\",\n     \"given\": \"The database is available and contains no request matching the submitted data.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client posts a valid request with padded title and description and valid caller-supplied id, createdAt, and status values.\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 201; the returned record has a positive system-generated id, UTC createdAt, trimmed title and description, status field \\\"Open\\\", and only fields allowed by the MaintenanceRequest schema; caller-supplied system-controlled values are not used.\",\n     \"level\": \"api\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"id\": \"AC-2.2\",\n     \"given\": \"The database is available and the request body has a valid title, area, and priority.\",\n  